  "Question": "Solve the system \\(\\begin{cases}x+2y=8\\\\3x-y=3\\end{cases}\\). (Write the values of \\(x\\) and \\(y\\), in that order, separated by a comma.)",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "2，3",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "From the first equation, \\(x=8-2y\\). Substitute into the second equation: \\(3(8-2y)-y=3\\), \\(24-7y=3\\), \\(y=3\\), \\(x=2\\).\n\nAlternative method 1: Double and add to eliminate y\n\nThe \\(y\\)-coefficients are \\(2\\) and \\(-1\\), so doubling the second equation makes them opposite. Adding the doubled equation to the first eliminates \\(y\\):\n\\[\n(x+2y)+2(3x-y)=8+2\\cdot3,\n\\qquad 7x=14.\n\\]\nThus \\(x=2\\). Substituting into the first equation gives \\(2+2y=8\\), so \\(y=3\\). Therefore, the answer in the requested order is \\(2,3\\).",
